{"page_content": "Calculation of the STP influent concentration\n\nFor local scale assessments, it is assumed that one point source is releasing its wastewater to one STP.\n\nIn some situations, removal in the sewer can be taken into account. This is the case for rapidly reacting substances, substances following fast abiotic degradation as well as for substances for which biodegradation in the sewer is proven by OECD 314 A or similar literature or monitoring data, when the release takes place to a municipal STP. If applicable, removal in the sewer will also be considered at reginal scale on the standard fraction (80%) connected to an STP. Sewer degradation is not taken into account for releases to an industrial (on site) STP. The following equation is to be used to calculate the sewer effluent concentration taking into account removal in the sewer:\n\nCsewering C - Tbe pr SeWeTe rf 1 + kdeQsewer . HRT sewer\n\nEquation R.16-17\n\nExplanation of symbols", "metadata": {"doc_id": "fee68a3f-301e-4668-bd1d-b9e05da43696", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}